  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Points \\((\\sqrt{\\pi}, a)\\) and \\((\\sqrt{\\pi}, b)\\) are distinct points on the graph of \\[y^2 + x^4 = 2x^2 y + 1.\\] What is \\(|a-b|?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt{1+\\pi}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(1 + \\sqrt{\\pi}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2015-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Substitute \\(x=\\sqrt{\\pi}\\). Then \\(x^2=\\pi\\) and \\(x^4=\\pi^2\\), so the equation becomes \\[y^2-2\\pi y+\\pi^2=1.\\]\n\nHence \\((y-\\pi)^2=1\\), giving the two possible values \\(y=\\pi+1\\) and \\(y=\\pi-1\\). Their distance is \\(2\\).\n\nThus, C is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute \\(x=\\sqrt{\\pi}\\) and complete a square in \\(y\\)",
        "The two \\(y\\)-values are symmetric around \\(\\pi\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
